==============================================================================
  9.  THE BROADBAND SESSION OFFSET THAT INVALIDATES THE NAIVE CW SIGMA
==============================================================================
  fan-on is uniformly ~0.9 dB BELOW fan-off in EVERY band from 20 Hz to
  25 kHz, including 10-25 kHz (62-155 m/s) where no physical fan signal
  can exist.  A frequency-independent offset across three decades is a
  receiver/session gain difference (different day, different noise floor),
  not a target.  Consequences:
    median fan-on minus fan-off over 20 Hz-25 kHz : -0.83 dB
    same for the second fan-on chunk               : -1.08 dB
    naive per-band sigma at 10-25 kHz              :  0.012 dB
    ACTUAL session-to-session offset               :  0.83 dB
  -> the honest CW floor is the ~0.9 dB session offset, roughly 70x the
     naive statistical sigma.  Any CW on/off band difference below ~1 dB
     is uninformative.  Corrected for the offset, every band is within
     +-0.15 dB of zero:
          20-   200 Hz : -0.14 dB after removing the -0.83 dB offset
         200-  1000 Hz : -0.16 dB after removing the -0.83 dB offset
        1000-  4000 Hz : -0.02 dB after removing the -0.83 dB offset
        4000- 10000 Hz : +0.01 dB after removing the -0.83 dB offset
       10000- 25000 Hz : -0.02 dB after removing the -0.83 dB offset

